@page
@model AboutModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}
<h1>About Practical Music</h1>
<p class="lead">Practical Music links PDF sheet music with audio recordings. Import a PDF and MP3s, mark where each page
    and each line starts in the recording, then play: the pages turn themselves and the part being played is highlighted.</p>

<div class="grid2">
    <div class="card">
        <h2>On this website</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Library</b> - your organization's books. Managers add PDFs, define the songs, add recordings and set the timing, just like in the app.</li>
            <li><b>Play</b> - one page in portrait, two in landscape; pages turn with the recording; tap a line to jump there. Keys: Space play/pause, ←/→ ±5 s, PageUp/PageDown turn pages, N/P next/previous song, F full display.</li>
            <li><b>Share</b> - lead a synchronized session, or follow whoever leads. Browsers and the apps play in sync through this website.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
        <h2>iPhone and iPad</h2>
        <p>No App Store needed: open this website in <b>Safari</b>, tap <b>Share</b> → <b>Add to Home Screen</b>. Practical Music then starts full screen like an app.</p>
        <p>Before following a leader, tap the page once so the browser allows the recording to play by itself.</p>
        <h2>Windows, Linux and Android</h2>
        <p>The apps work on their own and on the local network. Sign in on their <b>Online</b> page to download your organization's books, upload changes (managers) and sync with everyone here. <a href="/Downloads">Downloads</a></p>
    </div>
</div>

<h2>Credits</h2>
<p>Author: <b>Russ Judge</b>. Built with the assistance of Claude (Anthropic). Version @Model.Version.</p>
<p class="muted">Open source components: ASP.NET Core (MIT), PDFium (BSD-3), MailKit/MimeKit (MIT), MySqlConnector (MIT), Dapper (Apache 2.0); in the apps also Avalonia UI (MIT), LibVLC (LGPL-2.1), CommunityToolkit.Mvvm (MIT).</p>

